# DECISION LOG
## ECE-050 – Component Tolerance Checker and Batch Acceptance Engine

**Team ID:** E018  
**Institution:** Atria Institute of Technology  
**Academic Year:** 2026–2027  

### 1. Purpose
This Decision Log records the major technical and design decisions made during the development of the Component Tolerance Checker and Batch Acceptance Engine.

### 2. Project Decisions

| No. | Decision | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Python was selected as the programming language. | Python provides simple syntax and supports rapid application development. |
| 2 | Flask was selected for web application development. | Flask is lightweight and suitable for building the project's web interface. |
| 3 | MySQL was selected as the database. | MySQL provides structured storage and retrieval of inspection records. |
| 4 | VS Code was selected as the development environment. | It supports Python development, extensions and integrated terminal access. |
| 5 | A tolerance-based PASS/FAIL evaluation method was implemented. | It determines whether a measured component value is within the permitted tolerance range. |
| 6 | Inclusive boundary checking was implemented. | Measurements exactly equal to the minimum or maximum permitted values should be accepted. |
| 7 | Inspection history was implemented. | It allows users to retrieve previously saved inspection records. |
| 8 | Batch processing was implemented. | It allows multiple component measurements to be evaluated together. |
| 9 | SI engineering-prefix parsing was included. | It supports component values expressed using prefixes such as k, M, m, µ, n and p. |
| 10 | Invalid batch measurements are classified as SKIP. | Invalid values should not be incorrectly classified as PASS or FAIL. |
| 11 | Excel report generation was implemented. | It allows users to download inspection and batch measurement results. |
| 12 | Automated testing was performed using pytest. | It helps verify application behaviour and identify errors. |

### 3. Testing Decision

The project was verified using automated tests.

- Evaluation tests: 19 passed.
- Application tests: 16 passed.
- Total automated tests: 35 passed.

Database-backed batch processing and Excel report generation were also verified.

### 4. Final Technical Decision

The team decided to use a Python Flask application connected to a MySQL database to provide manual inspection, batch measurement evaluation, inspection history and downloadable reports.

### 5. Conclusion

The decisions recorded above guided the development of the project and helped establish a functional, testable and maintainable component tolerance checking system.

